! jb_ax5b "I-Box 5" -- THE BIT TABLE and the constant pool it sits in
! (PDF pp.114-115, octal 024501.00-024621.00, 81 rows), plus the
! deck's SYN table and END (PDF p.116, no storage).  Transcribed at
! the listing's own addresses and checked bit-exactly by
! verify_ax5b_bit_table_listing.py.
!
! CITED BY PDF PAGE.  These listing pages carry no printed page
! numbers; the "12 11 10 9" down the left margin is fanfold
! carriage-tape line numbering.  Every page image below was rendered
! with pdftoppm at 400 dpi and, where a glyph mattered, at 600 dpi.
!
! ====================================================================
! PREMISE CHECK, run before a line was written.
!
! Every octal address from 024501 to 024621 was grepped against every
! strap/verify_*.py and every strap/programs/*.strap.  RESULT: NOT ONE
! OF THEM APPEARS IN A ROWS ENTRY ANYWHERE.  The distinction matters,
! so here is the exact split:
!   * The only ROWS tuple anywhere in the 0245xx neighbourhood is
!     verify_ax5b_1274_truncation_listing.py:587,
!         ('024500.00', '0.00 00 000000.00 00', 'I74PSI XW,0,0,0'),
!     which is 024500 -- ONE WORD BELOW this block, and the last row
!     of routine 1274.
!   * 024522 (BIT0) appears in ax5b_1258_test1.strap:251,
!     ax5b_1268_tail_pool.strap, ax5b_1274_truncation's docstring and
!     header, verify_ax5b_16087_listing.py's injection table, and
!     several prose paragraphs.  Every one is a SYN line, an operand
!     of some OTHER row, or prose.
!   * 024534/024535 (BIT10/BIT11), 024543 (BIT17), 024613 (BIT57),
!     024620/024621 (BIT62/BIT63) appear only in docstring prose in
!     verify_ax5b_160_test8b, _160_test7_sweep, _160102, _162_test3b.
!   * 024501 (I00LC), 024502 (I00Z), 024503 (I00O) appear only as SYN
!     inputs and prose (ax5b_160_test6, ax5b_1683, ax5b_1274).
! verify_ax5b_1268_test1bc_listing.py:405 states the gap outright:
! "this repository has a ROWS entry on p.114's BIT table."  It did
! not.  It does now: 81 checked rows, 82 symbol assertions and one END
! assertion.
!
! ====================================================================
! THE HEADING, VERBATIM, WITH ITS OCTAL NEIGHBOURS.
!
! PDF p.114, immediately after routine 1274's last word (I74PSI
! "XW,0,0,0" at 024500.00) and before the pool's first row, the
! listing prints, in the comment column, with NO location and NO
! machine code:
!
!         -COMMON CONSTANTS FOR FETCH ONLY
!
! then a bare "-" comment row, then "SENO  SYN,SEN0" (no location
! either: a SYN occupies no storage), then I00LC at 024501.00.
!
! THE NEGATIVE, WHICH MATTERS AS MUCH: the BIT table has NO banner of
! its own.  Between the last anonymous zero word (024521.00) and BIT0
! (024522.00) there is exactly one bare "-" comment row and nothing
! else.  "BIT0..BIT63" is a sub-block of -COMMON CONSTANTS FOR FETCH
! ONLY, not a titled table.
!
! ====================================================================
! QUESTION 1: IS THE RULE EXACTLY 024522 + n, FOR ALL 64?
!
! YES.  Checked ROW BY ROW against the listing's own LOCATION column,
! not at the endpoints:
!
!   PDF p.114  BIT0  024522.00 ... BIT35 024565.00   36 rows
!   PDF p.115  BIT36 024566.00 ... BIT63 024621.00   28 rows
!
! 0o24565 - 0o24522 = 0o43 = 35, so p.114's 36 rows are unbroken.
! 0o24621 - 0o24566 = 0o33 = 27, so p.115's 28 rows are unbroken.
! 0o24621 - 0o24522 = 0o77 = 63 across the page break.  No gap, no
! repeat, no off-by-one anywhere.  All 64 locations are asserted
! individually in the verify script's SYMBOLS.
!
! A SECOND, INDEPENDENT SEAL ON THE ENDS.  PDF p.116 prints
! "END,(8)14000.0" against location 024622.00.  024622 = BIT63 + 1,
! so nothing was omitted between BIT63 and the end of the deck; and
! 024501 = I74PSI's 024500 + 1, so nothing was omitted at the top
! either.  The block is closed on both sides by printed locations.
!
! ====================================================================
! QUESTION 2: DOES BIT<n> HOLD BIT n?  YES -- AND THE BLOCK IS NOT
! 64 XWs.  THAT IS THE MORE INTERESTING RESULT.
!
! Every one of the 64 printed machine-code values decodes to exactly
! one set bit, at IBM bit n.  But the table reaches those 64 bits
! through FIVE different XW fields, and at one row it cannot use XW
! at all:
!
!   rows      field that carries the bit         printed where
!   BIT0-23   VALUE  (mag, packed << 40)         first half, VVVVVV.VV
!   BIT24     the SIGN bit -- via DD, NOT XW     22 octal digits
!   BIT25-27  the 3-bit FLAG operand (<< 36)     first half, hex pair
!   BIT28-45  COUNT (<< 18)                      spans both halves
!   BIT46-63  REFILL                             second half
!
! THE BIT24 EXCEPTION AND WHY IT IS FORCED.  IBM bit 24 of an index
! word is the VALUE field's SIGN.  In STRAP's "XW,VALUE,COUNT,REFILL,
! FLAG" there is no operand that sets it alone: the sign comes only
! from a negative VALUE, and a negative VALUE also writes magnitude
! bits 0-23.  A word with bit 24 set and nothing else is therefore
! UNREACHABLE through XW's operand syntax, and the programmer dropped
! to a raw data definition for that one row:
!
!   BIT24   (8)DD(BU),0 000 000 010 000 000 000 000
!                                     0000000010000000000000
!
! I00VO on the same page is the control: "XW,(8)-777777.77,0,0"
! prints "777777.77 80 000000.00 00" -- sign bit set, but with all 24
! magnitude bits set alongside it, which is exactly why BIT24 could
! not be written that way.
!
! The four printed values the brief named, read here at 600 dpi:
!   BIT0   XW,(8)400000.00,0,0   -> 400000.00 00 000000.00 00
!   BIT17  XW,(8)1.00,0,0        ->      1.00 00 000000.00 00
!   BIT32  XW,0,8192,0           ->      0.00 00 400000.00 00
!   BIT63  XW,0,0,1              ->      0.00 00 000000.00 01
! and the cross-check the brief offered is confirmed on the page:
!   BIT16  XW,(8)2.00,0,0        ->      2.00 00 000000.00 00
!   BIT17  XW,(8)1.00,0,0        ->      1.00 00 000000.00 00
!
! ====================================================================
! WHAT IS NOT VERBATIM HERE, AND WHY.  THREE ROWS, NAMED.
!
! The rule is "keep source rows verbatim".  Three printed rows cannot
! be written as printed, because strap_asm.py's grammar is narrower
! than STRAP-1's.  Each printed form is quoted beside its row above
! and in the verify script's note column; the transformations are:
!
!  1. "(8)DD(BU,64,8),0 000 011 770 025 700 000 000"  (I00LC) and
!     "(8)DD(BU,64,8),1777777777777777777777"         (I00O) and
!     "(8)DD(BU),0 000 000 010 000 000 000 000"       (BIT24)
!     print the radix entry "(8)" as a prefix on the whole STATEMENT.
!     strap_asm.py's _TERM_RADIX accepts "(R)" only on a numeric TERM
!     (C22-6531 pp.27-28), so it is moved onto the operand and the
!     listing's digit grouping spaces are closed up:
!         DD(BU,64,8),(8)0000011770025700000000
!         DD(BU,64,8),(8)1777777777777777777777
!         DD(BU),(8)0000000010000000000000
!     The DIGITS are untouched, and the printed machine code checks
!     them.
!  2. "XW,(8)-777777.77,0,0" (I00VO) puts the minus AFTER the radix
!     entry.  _TERM_RADIX is r'\((\d+)\)(?=[\d.])' -- it requires a
!     digit or a dot next, so "(8)-" does not match.  Written here as
!     "XW,-(8)777777.77,0,0".  Same value, same printed word
!     (777777.77 80 000000.00 00).
!
! WHAT *IS* KEPT, THOUGH IT LOOKS LIKE A TYPO: BIT18/19/20 print
! ".40" / ".20" / ".10" with NO leading zero, while BIT21/22/23 print
! "0.04" / "0.02" / "0.01" WITH one.  That is the deck's own
! keypunching, it is reproduced here unchanged, and it assembles to
! the same values either way.
!
! ====================================================================
! WITNESS TIERING.  What this file proves, and what it does not.
!
! TIER 1, WITNESSED -- the 81 printed machine-code words.  Every row
! below has its own value in the listing's machine-code column, read
! row by row off pp.114-115.  These are 81 independent data.
!
! TIER 1, WITNESSED -- the 64 BIT<n> LOCATIONS.  pp.114-115 print a
! location column of their own, and all 64 were read from it
! separately from the machine code.  Those 64 printed locations, not
! the location counter, are what establish "BIT<n> = 024522 + n".
!
! TIER 2, ANCHOR, NOT EVIDENCE -- the single "SLC,(8)24501.0".  From
! that one number the assembler derives all 81 locations by size
! accounting (XW = 64 bits aligned full-word; DD(BU,64,8) with k
! operands = 64k bits).  A label placed by the location counter is
! NOT a witness to its own address.  What the verify script actually
! checks is the AGREEMENT between that propagation and the location
! column read independently off the page -- 64 separate equalities.
! With 64 near-identical consecutive XWs, one SLC plus the counter
! does nearly all of the address arithmetic; the page is what makes
! it a check rather than an assumption.  If the SLC is wrong by one
! word, ALL 81 rows and ALL 69 location symbols fail together; that
! is injection 7 below, and it is recorded precisely because it
! proves so little.
!
! TIER 3, DERIVED BY ARITHMETIC, NOT READ -- the 3-words-per-statement
! split of the four anonymous "DD(BU,64,8),0,0,0" rows.  The listing
! prints four source lines and twelve machine-code lines
! (024506.00-024521.00); 12 / 4 = 3 matches the three operands each
! line carries.  The individual boundaries between the four groups
! were NOT read off the page -- the source lines sit between code
! rows, not level with them.  Those twelve rows are also label-free,
! and their printed value is 22 zeros, so they are the weakest tier
! here.  They are included because the location column is printed for
! every one of them and because they are what puts BIT0 at 024522.
!
! TIER 4, INPUTS, NOT WITNESSES -- nothing.  This file SYNs no symbol
! from outside itself.  Every symbol it defines comes from a row on
! pp.114-116.
!
! PROMOTED FROM INPUT TO CHECKED -- the p.116 SYN table.  SEN, SEN0,
! SERS, SSW, RET, RET1, RET2, ERS, INT, IDF1, IDF2, DPET13 are pure
! assumed inputs in nearly every other transcription in this repo
! (ax5b_1274_truncation.strap:393-399, ax5b_1268_tail_pool.strap:
! 434-440, ax5b_1258_test1.strap:249-253, ax4b_1246_*.strap, ...).
! Here they are transcribed from p.116's SOURCE column and checked
! against p.116's VALUE column -- two different printed columns, so
! the assertion is a real (if narrow) check of STRAP's evaluation,
! not an input.  verify_ax5b_1274_truncation_listing.py:158 already
! QUOTED this table in prose and said "Corroboration, not promotion";
! this is the promotion.
!
! ====================================================================
! SENO / SEN0: THE ALIAS, SETTLED.
!
! PDF p.114's first pool row prints
!
!     SENO    SYN,SEN0                1311.00+   +00000000
!
! Three independent lines, all agreeing:
!  1. Same printed ROW, 600 dpi: the LABEL's 4th glyph measures 54 px,
!     the OPERAND's 4th measures 42 px.  Digit zeros on the very next
!     row (I00LC) measure 48 and 45.  Letter O runs 15-22 % wider
!     than digit 0 on this deck (docs/listing_typography.md Sec.6).
!  2. PDF p.116, 600 dpi: "SEN0  SYN,(8)1311.0" -- the LABEL's 4th
!     glyph measures 44 px, a digit zero.
!  3. GLYPH-FREE, and this is the decisive one: p.114's row prints the
!     VALUE 1311.00+, and p.116 DEFINES SEN0 as (8)1311.0 = 1311.00+.
!     A symbol cannot be SYN'd to itself -- the definition would be
!     circular and could not have produced a printed value at all.
!     The two spellings must differ, and p.116 supplies the one the
!     operand names.
!
! So the row is an ALIAS: letter-O SENO defined as digit-zero SEN0.
! docs/listing_typography.md Sec.6 calls this "moderate, direction
! only"; with p.116's definition in hand it is settled for this row.
! ax5b_1258_test2.strap's "SENO SYN,SENO" (a self-SYN) is wrong.
! Both spellings are defined below, as the page defines them.
!
! BIT0 IS A DIGIT ZERO, not a letter O: its 4th glyph measures 45 px
! against 45-50 px for the five digit zeros in its own operand on the
! same printed row, and against 54 px for SENO's letter O eighteen
! rows above.  "BITO" would in any case be the odd one out in a
! series that runs to BIT63.
!
! I00O, NOT I000.  The all-ones row's 4th glyph measures 51 px
! against 43 and 42 px for the two digit zeros in the SAME token --
! ratio 1.20, squarely in the letter-O band.  I00VO ends 51 px and
! I00CO ends 55 px on the same page, both letter O.  The row's own
! comment is "-INDX WD. OF ONES." and its neighbour I00Z is
! "-ZERO INDX WD.", so O is for Ones and Z is for Zero.  This
! reproduces verify_ax5b_160_test8b_listing.py:103-105 independently.
! A DELIBERATE DEPARTURE, FLAGGED: the task that produced this file
! specified "I000" and said a repo-wide rename had applied it.  This
! file writes I00O instead, on the measurement above.
! docs/listing_typography.md Sec.5 lists the pool as "I00LC, I00Z,
! I000, I00VO, I00CO", but Sec.5's rename was about the LEADING glyph
! and it never measured the trailing one.
! verify_ax5b_1683_listing.py:53 also writes "I000".  The repo
! majority (12 files) already writes I00O.
!
! ====================================================================
! FIRST FOR THIS REPO: ONE, after grep knocked out two candidates.
!
!  * "DD(BU)" WITH NO LENGTH OR PADDING MODIFIER -- BIT24.  The grep
!    was run BEFORE this file existed: `grep -rn 'DD(BU)' strap/`,
!    zero hits, and `grep -rnE 'DD *\( *BU *\)' strap/` for the
!    spacing variants, zero hits.  Every other DD in the repo writes
!    DD(BU,64,8) or DD(BU,32,8).  (Running it now will of course find
!    this file.)  strap_asm.dds_length_bits defaults a missing length
!    to 64, which is what makes the row assemble to a full word;
!    before this file nothing exercised that default.
!
!  KNOCKED OUT (claimed, then eliminated by grep):
!  * "XW with a non-zero FOURTH operand" (BIT25/26/27).  NOT a first:
!    programs/ibox1_bind.strap:79 already assembles "IBXWZO
!    XW,-1,0,0,4", and strap_asm.py's own comment names
!    op_ad_indicators.strap's WOTHER.
!  * "SYN whose operand is another symbol" (SENO SYN,SEN0).  NOT a
!    first: programs/dcp_maintenance_compool.strap:104 already has
!    "EBAUTO SYN, ECTL1", and eleven more like it.
!
! ====================================================================
! PROVEN DISCRIMINATING.  Ten injections into strap_asm.py, with the
! OBSERVED failing rows, are tabulated in
! verify_ax5b_bit_table_listing.py's docstring.  The short version:
! seven are discriminating and three of those move exactly ONE row
! (BIT24 alone, I00VO alone, BIT46 alone); one is the deliberately
! weak "shift the SLC" injection, recorded because it moves 139 of
! 164 checks identically and therefore distinguishes nothing; and two
! are genuine nulls with their arithmetic reasons.  Baseline: 164 checks,
! 0 failures, ALL TESTS PASSED.

! ====================================================================
! THE TRANSCRIPTION.  One SLC, then every statement in printed order.
! ====================================================================
        SLC,(8)24501.0      ! PDF p.114's own location column: I00LC
!
! -COMMON CONSTANTS FOR FETCH ONLY          <- the pool banner, printed
!                                              with no location and no
!                                              machine code
! -                                         <- a bare comment row
SENO    SYN,SEN0            ! p.114: "SENO   SYN,SEN0" -> 1311.00+
I00LC   DD(BU,64,8),(8)0000011770025700000000
!                             p.114: "(8)DD(BU,64,8),0 000 011 770 025
!                             700 000 000"   0000011770025700000000
I00Z    XW,0,0,0,0          ! p.114: "-ZERO INDX WD."
I00O    DD(BU,64,8),(8)1777777777777777777777
!                             p.114: "(8)DD(BU,64,8),1777777777777777
!                             777777-INDX WD. OF ONES."
I00VO   XW,-(8)777777.77,0,0
!                             p.114: "XW,(8)-777777.77,0,0"
I00CO   XW,0,(8)777777,0    ! p.114: "XW,0,(8)777777,0"
!
! Four anonymous DD(BU,64,8),0,0,0 statements, three words each:
! 024506.00-024521.00, twelve zero words, no labels at all.
        DD(BU,64,8),0,0,0
        DD(BU,64,8),0,0,0
        DD(BU,64,8),0,0,0
        DD(BU,64,8),0,0,0
!
! -                                         <- a bare comment row, the
!                                              only thing between the
!                                              pool and BIT0: the bit
!                                              table has NO banner
BIT0    XW,(8)400000.00,0,0
BIT1    XW,(8)200000.00,0,0
BIT2    XW,(8)100000.00,0,0
BIT3    XW,(8)40000.00,0,0
BIT4    XW,(8)20000.00,0,0
BIT5    XW,(8)10000.00,0,0
BIT6    XW,(8)4000.00,0,0
BIT7    XW,(8)2000.00,0,0
BIT8    XW,(8)1000.00,0,0
BIT9    XW,(8)400.00,0,0
BIT10   XW,(8)200.00,0,0
BIT11   XW,(8)100.00,0,0
BIT12   XW,(8)40.00,0,0
BIT13   XW,(8)20.00,0,0
BIT14   XW,(8)10.00,0,0
BIT15   XW,(8)4.00,0,0
BIT16   XW,(8)2.00,0,0
BIT17   XW,(8)1.00,0,0
BIT18   XW,(8).40,0,0
BIT19   XW,(8).20,0,0
BIT20   XW,(8).10,0,0
BIT21   XW,(8)0.04,0,0
BIT22   XW,(8)0.02,0,0
BIT23   XW,(8)0.01,0,0
BIT24   DD(BU),(8)0000000010000000000000
BIT25   XW,0,0,0,4
BIT26   XW,0,0,0,2
BIT27   XW,0,0,0,1
BIT28   XW,0,131072,0
BIT29   XW,0,65536,0
BIT30   XW,0,32768,0
BIT31   XW,0,16384,0
BIT32   XW,0,8192,0
BIT33   XW,0,4096,0
BIT34   XW,0,2048,0
BIT35   XW,0,1024,0
BIT36   XW,0,512,0
BIT37   XW,0,256,0
BIT38   XW,0,128,0
BIT39   XW,0,64,0
BIT40   XW,0,32,0
BIT41   XW,0,16,0
BIT42   XW,0,8,0
BIT43   XW,0,4,0
BIT44   XW,0,2,0
BIT45   XW,0,1,0
BIT46   XW,0,0,131072
BIT47   XW,0,0,65536
BIT48   XW,0,0,32768
BIT49   XW,0,0,16384
BIT50   XW,0,0,8192
BIT51   XW,0,0,4096
BIT52   XW,0,0,2048
BIT53   XW,0,0,1024
BIT54   XW,0,0,512
